  "answer": "Not all checks pass. The build passed, but the unit tests failed, so the component stage was skipped. I didn't modify any files.\n\n| Stage | Result |\n|---|---|\n| build (`make build`) | passed |\n| unit (`make unit`) | **failed**, exit code 2 |\n| component (`make component`) | skipped, because the run halted at the unit failure |\n\nThe integration and skills stages weren't part of the configured run.\n\n**Unit test failures**\n\nThe log shows 39 failures out of 272 tests (233 passed). The log lists 78 `Failed` lines because the suite ran twice, once on each target framework (net9.0 and net10.0). All the failures come from one cause: the semantic matcher doesn't recognise its own built-in matcher names. `SemanticMatcher.Apply` (`src/ConfIT/Matching/SemanticMatcher.cs:line 61`) throws on every name, and the names it reports are all lowercase (`isnull`, `isuuid`, `greaterthan`). That looks like a case-sensitivity problem in how matcher names are looked up or normalised. I haven't confirmed that in the source.\n\n- **Unknown matcher name (35 of 39):**\n  - Quoted error: `System.ArgumentException : Unknown semantic matcher 'isuuid' for field 'id'`\n  - Other names reported: `isnull`, `isnotnull`, `greaterthan`, `lessthan`.\n  - Most are in `SemanticMatcherTests`, for example `Apply_IsUuidWithInvalidValue_ReturnsFailure` and `Apply_IsEmailWithValidEmail_Passes`.\n  - `Apply_CustomMatcherName_DelegatesToCustomFunc` also fails, so custom-matcher dispatch is probably affected too.\n- **Passing tests that now throw (1 of 39):**\n  - Test: `ResultMatcherTests.MatchResponseBody_NullExpectedWithSemanticMatcher_DoesNotThrow`.\n  - Quoted error: `Did not expect any exception, but found System.ArgumentException: Unknown semantic matcher '<name>' for field '<field>'`.\n  - `SemanticMatcherTests.Apply_NullExpected_DoesNotThrow` appears to fit this group as well, but I didn't confirm its message.\n- **Wrong exception type (1 of 39):**\n  - Test: `SemanticMatcherTests.Apply_FieldAbsentFromResponse_ThrowsInvalidOperationException`.\n  - Quoted error: `Expected a <System.InvalidOperationException> to be thrown, but found <System.ArgumentException>:`\n  - The unknown-matcher error is raised before the missing-field check.\n\nThe log is at `tmp/verification/20261021T073319Z-defa8d/unit.log`.\n\nSince component tests were skipped, their status is unknown until the unit failure is fixed.",
